.TH mnnn-rule-create 1  "mnnn-rule-create 2.13.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-rule\-create \- Create a rule
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn rule create\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-on\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-if\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-then\fR] [\fB\-\-project\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-journal\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-search\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-model\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-related\fR] [\fB\-\-disabled\fR] [\fB\-\-description\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a rule
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-on\fR \fI<KIND>\fR
Action kinds to react to: import, journal.*, * (repeat or comma\-separate)
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-if\fR \fI<CONDITION>\fR
A condition: FIELD OP VALUE, e.g. "inserted > 0" (repeat: all must hold)
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-then\fR \fI<ACTION>\fR
A then\-action, e.g. "status Imported {inserted} bars" (repeat: run in order)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
Put it in a project (as a project item)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-journal\fR \fI<JOURNAL>\fR
Let it live in a journal (its default journal)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-search\fR \fI<SEARCH>\fR
Let it live in a live search (its default search)
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
Let it live in a model (its default model for record\-… and model\-… actions)
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-related\fR
Only react to actions about where it lives
.TP
\fB\-\-disabled\fR
Create it switched off
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR [default: ]

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>

.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v2.13.0
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmnnn\fR(1)
